                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integration"} integration
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+vector+space"} topological vector space
                  %h2#basic_facts Basic facts
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+metric+space+valued+function+on+compact+metric+space+is+uniformly+continuous"} continuous metric space valued function on compact metric space is uniformly continuous
                  %p …
                  %h2#theorems Theorems
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intermediate+value+theorem"} intermediate value theorem
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extreme+value+theorem"} extreme value theorem
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heine-Borel+theorem"} Heine-Borel theorem
                  %p …
          %h1#section_table_of_contents Contents
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#definitions"} Definitions
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#as_a_terminal_object"} As a terminal object
              %li
                %a{:href => "#properties"} Properties
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#algebraic_structure_on_real_numbers"} Algebraic structure on real numbers
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_concepts"} Related concepts
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            There are many possible definitions of the (two-sided, Dedekind) real numbers type in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+universe"} type universe
            or a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+of+all+propositions"} type of all propositions
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dedekind+real+numbers"} Dedekind real numbers
            over to dependent type theory.
          %p
            However, in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
            without a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+universe"} type universe
            or a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+of+all+propositions"} type of all propositions
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dedekind+real+numbers"} Dedekind real numbers
            no longer works. Nonetheless, it is possible to define the type of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inference+rules"} inference rules
            as a type with a type family of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/domains"} domains
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structural+Dedekind+cut"} structural Dedekind cut
            associated with each
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+number"} real number
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %p
            We shall assume the minimum amount of type formers in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
            to define
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dedekind+cuts"} Dedekind cuts
            of the rational numbers:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+product+types"}> dependent product types
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+sum+types"} dependent sum types
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+types"} identity types
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+type"} empty type
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+type"} unit type
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sum+types"} sum types
              or
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/booleans"} booleans
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝟚
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{2}
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bracket+types"} bracket types
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers+type"} natural numbers type
          %p
            The types in the dependent type theory form the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category+theory"} (infinity,1)-categorical
            version of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heyting+category"} Heyting category
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exponential+objects"} exponential objects
            and a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers+object"} natural numbers object
          %p
            In addition, if one has a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+of+all+propositions"} type of all propositions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Prop
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Prop}
            in the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subtypes"} subtypes
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/predicates"} predicates
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝟚
                  %mo ×
                  %mi ℚ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Prop
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C:(\mathbb{2} \times \mathbb{Q}) \to \mathrm{Prop}
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+type"} product type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝟚
                  %mo ×
                  %mi ℚ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{2} \times \mathbb{Q}
            which satisfy the following axioms:
          %ul
            %li
              %p Dedekind cuts are bounded:
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ∃
                      %mi q
                      %mo :
                      %mi ℚ
                      %mo .
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mi q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                      %mo ∃
                      %mi r
                      %mo :
                      %mi ℚ
                      %mo .
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi r
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \exists q:\mathbb{Q}.C(0, q) \quad \exists r:\mathbb{Q}.C(1, r)
            %li
              %p Dedekind cuts are rounded:
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                        %mrow
                          %mi q
                          %mo :
                          %mi ℚ
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mi q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≃
                      %mo ∃
                      %mi r
                      %mo :
                      %mi ℚ
                      %mo .
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi q
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi r
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ×
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mi r
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \prod_{q:\mathbb{Q}} C(0, q)) \simeq \exists r:\mathbb{Q}.(q \lt r) \times C(0, r))
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                        %mrow
                          %mi r
                          %mo :
                          %mi ℚ
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi r
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≃
                      %mo ∃
                      %mi q
                      %mo :
                      %mi ℚ
                      %mo .
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi q
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi r
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ×
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \prod_{r:\mathbb{Q}} C(1, r)) \simeq \exists q:\mathbb{Q}.(q \lt r) \times C(1, q))
            %li
              %p Dedekind cuts are disjoint:
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                        %mrow
                          %mi q
                          %mo :
                          %mi ℚ
                      %mo ¬
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mi q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ×
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \prod_{q:\mathbb{Q}} \neg (C(0, q)) \times C(1, q)))
            %li
              %p Dedekind cuts are located:
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                        %mrow
                          %mi q
                          %mo :
                          %mi ℚ
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                        %mrow
                          %mi r
                          %mo :
                          %mi ℚ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi q
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi r
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mi q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∨
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi r
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \prod_{q:\mathbb{Q}} \prod_{r:\mathbb{Q}} (q \lt r) \to (C(0, q)) \vee C(1, r))
          %p
            Usually, Dedekind cuts are presented as pairs of predicates
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi L
                    %mo ,
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℚ
                    %mo →
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Prop
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℚ
                    %mo →
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Prop
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (L, U):(\mathbb{Q} \to \mathrm{Prop}) \times (\mathbb{Q} \to \mathrm{Prop})
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo +
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ((A + B) \to C) \simeq (A \to C) \times (B \to C)
          %p
            and for any type
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo +
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝟚
                  %mo ×
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A + A) \simeq (\mathbb{2} \times A)
          %p
            The predicate
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} isCut
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{isCut}(C)
            is defined as the product of all the axioms above, and the type of real numbers is defined as
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo ≔
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo :
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝟚
                      %mo ×
                      %mi ℚ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Prop
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} isCut
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R} \coloneqq \sum_{C:(\mathbb{2} \times \mathbb{Q}) \to \mathrm{Prop}} \mathrm{isCut}(C)
          %p
            In dependent type theory with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+universe"} type universe
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            = succeed "-small" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Prop
                    %mi U
                  %mo ≔
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo :
                      %mi U
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} isProp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Prop}_U \coloneqq \sum_{A:U} \mathrm{isProp}(A)
          %p
            and define locally
            = succeed "-small" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝟚
                  %mo ×
                  %mi ℚ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Prop
                    %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C:(\mathbb{2} \times \mathbb{Q}) \to \mathrm{Prop}_U
            and the (locally
            = succeed "-small)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}_U
            using
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Prop
                      %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Prop}_U
          %p
            So, what happens if the dependent type theory has neither a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+of+all+propositions"} type of all propositions
            nor a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+universe"} type universe
            = succeed "?" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/predicative+mathematics"} predicative mathematics
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝟚
                    %mo ×
                    %mi ℚ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{2} \times \mathbb{Q}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subtype"} subtype
            of the sum type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝟚
                  %mo ×
                  %mi ℚ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{2} \times \mathbb{Q}
            is a type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            with an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/embedding+of+types"} embedding of types
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi e
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo ↪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝟚
                    %mo ×
                    %mi ℚ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e:C \hookrightarrow (\mathbb{2} \times \mathbb{Q})
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo :
                    %mi 𝟚
                    %mo ×
                    %mi ℚ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:\mathbb{2} \times \mathbb{Q}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+type"} fiber type
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi e
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
            at
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mere+proposition"} mere proposition
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} isProp
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi z
                        %mo :
                        %mi C
                    %mi e
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo =
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝟚
                        %mo ×
                        %mi ℚ
                    %mi x
                    %mo )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{isProp}\left(\sum_{z:C} e(z) =_{\mathbb{2} \times \mathbb{Q}} x\right)
          %p
            so everywhere in the definition above where one would have used the type family
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(x)
            one can instead use the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+sum+type"} dependent sum type
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} fiber
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi e
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi z
                        %mo :
                        %mi C
                    %mi e
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo =
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝟚
                        %mo ×
                        %mi ℚ
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{fiber}(e, x) \coloneqq \sum_{z:C} e(z) =_{\mathbb{2} \times \mathbb{Q}} x
          %p
            Then a Dedekind cut consists of a type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            with an embedding of types
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi e
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo ↪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝟚
                    %mo ×
                    %mi ℚ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e:C \hookrightarrow (\mathbb{2} \times \mathbb{Q})
          %ul
            %li
              %p Dedekind cuts are bounded:
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ∃
                      %mi q
                      %mo :
                      %mi ℚ
                      %mo .
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} fiber
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi e
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mi q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                      %mo ∃
                      %mi r
                      %mo :
                      %mi ℚ
                      %mo .
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} fiber
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi e
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi r
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \exists q:\mathbb{Q}.\mathrm{fiber}(e, (0, q)) \quad \exists r:\mathbb{Q}.\mathrm{fiber}(e, (1, r))
            %li
              %p Dedekind cuts are rounded:
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                        %mrow
                          %mi q
                          %mo :
                          %mi ℚ
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} fiber
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi e
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mi q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≃
                      %mo ∃
                      %mi r
                      %mo :
                      %mi ℚ
                      %mo .
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi q
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi r
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ×
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} fiber
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi e
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mi r
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \prod_{q:\mathbb{Q}} \mathrm{fiber}(e, (0, q)) \simeq \exists r:\mathbb{Q}.(q \lt r) \times \mathrm{fiber}(e, (0, r))
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                        %mrow
                          %mi r
                          %mo :
                          %mi ℚ
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} fiber
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi e
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi r
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≃
                      %mo ∃
                      %mi q
                      %mo :
                      %mi ℚ
                      %mo .
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi q
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi r
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ×
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} fiber
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi e
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \prod_{r:\mathbb{Q}} \mathrm{fiber}(e, (1, r)) \simeq \exists q:\mathbb{Q}.(q \lt r) \times \mathrm{fiber}(e, (1, q))
            %li
              %p Dedekind cuts are disjoint:
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                        %mrow
                          %mi q
                          %mo :
                          %mi ℚ
                      %mo ¬
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} fiber
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi e
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mi q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ×
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} fiber
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi e
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \prod_{q:\mathbb{Q}} \neg (\mathrm{fiber}(e, (0, q)) \times \mathrm{fiber}(e, (1, q)))
            %li
              %p Dedekind cuts are located:
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                        %mrow
                          %mi q
                          %mo :
                          %mi ℚ
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                        %mrow
                          %mi r
                          %mo :
                          %mi ℚ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi q
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi r
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} fiber
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi e
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mi q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∨
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} fiber
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi e
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi r
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \prod_{q:\mathbb{Q}} \prod_{r:\mathbb{Q}} (q \lt r) \to (\mathrm{fiber}(e, (0, q)) \vee \mathrm{fiber}(e, (1, r))
          %p
            The predicate
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} isCut
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi e
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{isCut}(C, e)
            is defined as the product of all the axioms above, and the type of all Dedekind cuts with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/domain"} domain
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is given by the dependent sum type
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Cuts
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi e
                      %mo :
                      %mi C
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi 𝟚
                      %mo ×
                      %mi ℚ
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} isCut
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi e
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Cuts}(C) \coloneqq \sum_{e:C \hookrightarrow \mathbb{2} \times \mathbb{Q}} \mathrm{isCut}(C, e)
          %p
            If there existed a type universe, one can simply define the real numbers as the type of Dedekind cuts in
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi U
                  %mo ≔
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo :
                      %mi U
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Cuts
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}_U \coloneqq \sum_{C:U} \mathrm{Cuts}(C)
          %p
            However, while there is no type universe
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            behaves as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+sum+type"} dependent sum type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo :
                      %mi U
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Cuts
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sum_{C:U} \mathrm{Cuts}(C)
            if the hypothetical
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            contained every single type in the type theory.
          %p Formation rules for the real numbers type:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ctx
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \; \mathrm{ctx}}{\Gamma \vdash \mathbb{R} \; \mathrm{type}}
          %p Introduction rules for real numbers type:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi C
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} inR
                        %mi C
                      %mo :
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Cuts
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash C \; \mathrm{type}}{\Gamma \vdash \mathrm{inR}_C:\mathrm{Cuts}(C) \to \mathbb{R}}
          %p Elimination rules for real numbers type:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ctx
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} CutDomain
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                  %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ctx
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} cut
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Cuts
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} CutDomain
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \; \mathrm{ctx}}{\Gamma, x:\mathbb{R} \vdash \mathrm{CutDomain}(x) \; \mathrm{type}} \quad \frac{\Gamma \; \mathrm{ctx}}{\Gamma, x:\mathbb{R} \vdash \mathrm{cut}(x):\mathrm{Cuts}(\mathrm{CutDomain}(x))}
          %p Computation rules for real numbers type:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi C
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                      %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                      %mi c
                      %mo :
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Cuts
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} CutDomain
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} inR
                        %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≡
                      %mi C
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                  %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi C
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                      %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                      %mi c
                      %mo :
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Cuts
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} cut
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} inR
                        %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≡
                      %mi c
                      %mo :
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Cuts
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash C \; \mathrm{type} \quad c:\mathrm{Cuts}(C)}{\Gamma \vdash \mathrm{CutDomain}(\mathrm{inR}_C(c)) \equiv C \; \mathrm{type}} \quad \frac{\Gamma \vdash C \; \mathrm{type} \quad c:\mathrm{Cuts}(C)}{\Gamma \vdash \mathrm{cut}(\mathrm{inR}_C(c)) \equiv c:\mathrm{Cuts}(C)}
          %p Uniqueness rules for real numbers type:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ctx
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} inR
                        %mrow
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} CutDomain
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} cut
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≡
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Cuts
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} CutDomain
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \; \mathrm{ctx}}{\Gamma, x:\mathbb{R} \vdash \mathrm{inR}_{\mathrm{CutDomain}(x)}(\mathrm{cut}(x)) \equiv x:\mathrm{Cuts}(\mathrm{CutDomain}(x))}
          %p
            The inference rules for the real numbers type imply that the real numbers type are a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tarski+universe"} Tarski universe
            with universal type family
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} CutDomain
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{CutDomain}(x)
            indexed by
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo :
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:\mathbb{R}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} CutDomain
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{CutDomain}(x)
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/domain"} domain
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dedekind+cut"} Dedekind cut
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} cut
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} CutDomain
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝟚
                  %mo ×
                  %mi ℚ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{cut}(x):\mathrm{CutDomain}(x) \hookrightarrow (\mathbb{2} \times \mathbb{Q})
          %p
            associated with the real number
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo :
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:\mathbb{R}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+universes"} type universes
            such as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+of+all+propositions"} type of all propositions
            or the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+of+finite+types"} type of finite types
          %h3#as_a_terminal_object As a terminal object
          %p
            An
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Archimedean+ordered+field"} Archimedean ordered field
            can be defined in any dependent type theory with the following types:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+product+types"}> dependent product types
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+sum+types"} dependent sum types
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+types"} identity types
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+type"} empty type
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+type"} unit type
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sum+types"} sum types
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bracket+types"} bracket types
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers+type"} natural numbers type
          %p
            Then the real numbers type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{R}
            is the homotopy terminal Archimedean ordered field.
          %p
            If the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
            has
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+sets"} quotient sets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{R}
            is Cauchy complete. From the definition of homotopy terminal Archimedean ordered field,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{R}
            is an algebra of the endofunctor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \mapsto \mathcal{C}(X)
            which takes Archimedean ordered fields
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to the Archimedean ordered field
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}(X)
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+classes"} equivalence classes
            of Cauchy sequences in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \mapsto \mathcal{C}(X)
            in the type of Archimedean ordered field is a Cauchy complete Archimedean ordered field.
          %p
            Similarly, if
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+sets"} power sets
            of Archimedean ordered fields exist, then it is provable that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{R}
            is Dedekind complete. From the definition of homotopy terminal Archimedean field,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{R}
            is an algebra of the endofunctor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi 𝒟
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \mapsto \mathcal{D}(X)
            which takes Archimedean ordered fields
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to the Archimedean ordered field
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}(X)
            of two-sided Dedekind cuts in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi 𝒟
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \mapsto \mathcal{D}(X)
            in the type of Archimedean ordered field is a Dedekind complete Archimedean ordered field.
          %p
            If a real numbers type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            as defined in the previous section also exists, then it is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subtype"} subtype
            of this real numbers type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            defined as the terminal Archimedean ordered field, since
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            is provably Archimedean ordered, and any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+homomorphisms"} ring homomorphisms
            between two field objects is an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/embedding+of+types"} embedding of types
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \to \mathbb{R}
          %h2#properties Properties
          %p The type of real numbers is the Coquand universe of all Dedekind cuts. Since real numbers and Dedekind cuts are interdefinable via the rules of Coquand universes, we shall just be directly defining the algebraic operations and order relations on Dedekind cuts; the corresponding operations on real numbers follow from the rules of Coquand universes.
          %h3#algebraic_structure_on_real_numbers Algebraic structure on real numbers
          %p
          .num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              Addition of two Dedekind cuts
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C, e_C)
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi D
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (D, e_D)
              is given by the type
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo +
                    %mi D
                    %mo ≔
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi b
                        %mo ,
                        %mi q
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo :
                        %mi 𝟚
                        %mo ×
                        %mi ℚ
                    %mo ∃
                    %mi r
                    %mo ,
                    %mi s
                    %mo :
                    %mi ℚ
                    %mo .
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} fiber
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo ,
                    %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ×
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} fiber
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mi D
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo ,
                    %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi q
                    %msub
                      %mo =
                      %mi ℚ
                    %mi r
                    %mo +
                    %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C + D \coloneqq \sum_{(b, q):\mathbb{2} \times \mathbb{Q}} \exists r, s:\mathbb{Q}.\mathrm{fiber}(e_C, (b, r)) \times \mathrm{fiber}(e_D, (b, s)) \times (q =_\mathbb{Q} r + s)
            %p
              with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/embedding"} embedding
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                        %mo +
                        %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e_{C + D}
              given by the first projection function of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+sum+type"} dependent sum type
              into the product type
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝟚
                      %mo ×
                      %mi ℚ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{2} \times \mathbb{Q}
          %p
            The swap function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} swap
                  %mo :
                  %mi 𝟚
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝟚
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{swap}:\mathbb{2} \to \mathbb{2}
            on the booleans is inductively defined by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} swap
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{swap}(0) \coloneqq 1
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} swap
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{swap}(1) \coloneqq 0
          %p
          .num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              The additive inverse of a Dedekind cut
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C, e_C)
              is given by the type
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mi C
                    %mo ≔
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi b
                        %mo ,
                        %mi q
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo :
                        %mi 𝟚
                        %mo ×
                        %mi ℚ
                    %mo ∃
                    %mi r
                    %mo :
                    %mi ℚ
                    %mo .
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} fiber
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} swap
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi q
                    %msub
                      %mo =
                      %mi ℚ
                    %mo −
                    %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} -C \coloneqq \sum_{(b, q):\mathbb{2} \times \mathbb{Q}} \exists r:\mathbb{Q}.\mathrm{fiber}(e_C, (\mathrm{swap}(b), r)) \times (q =_\mathbb{Q} -r)
            %p
              with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/embedding"} embedding
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e_{-C}
              given by the first projection function of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+sum+type"} dependent sum type
              into the product type
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝟚
                      %mo ×
                      %mi ℚ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{2} \times \mathbb{Q}
          %p With these operations, the real numbers form an abelian group.
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers+object"} real numbers object
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dedekind+real+numbers"} Dedekind real numbers
          %h2#references References
          %p For the impredicative definition of the real numbers using a type of propositions, as well as the algebraic operations and order relations for real numbers see section 11.2 of:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Univalent+Foundations+Project"}> Univalent Foundations Project
              , section 11.2 of
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Homotopy+Type+Theory+--+Univalent+Foundations+of+Mathematics"} Homotopy Type Theory – Univalent Foundations of Mathematics
